  "review_reasoning": [
    "Panic path uses no lock, allocator, task API, queue, peripheral I/O, formatter, stack walk or info->details callback. Bounds precede DRAM dereference; volatile bounded writes and final commit protect partially written record validity.",
    "First capture latch prevents recursive overwriting. A recursion interrupting an incomplete write may lose the record (unknown), and does not turn partial data into verified evidence.",
    "Query snapshot is copied once at normal startup, avoiding a multiwriter seqlock or panic-context lock. Current query identity and original panic identity are separate.",
    "CRC32 detects corruption; record identifier is not authentication. Register values require their known flags. Xtensa return address is raw ABI value.",
    "Last retained panic can predate the current reset, which the protocol explicitly distinguishes via origin session/boot/full ELF and current reset field."
  ],
